        "id": 0,
        "original_id": "3190814a-58e1-50cb-8116-ab5739c0481f",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Jane Mayer, Charles Koch, David Koch, the Koch family\n- Products: Dark Money: The Hidden History of the Billionaires Behind the Rise of the Radical Right\n- Companies: Koch Industries\n- Concepts: conservative libertarians, political activities, influence networks\n\nFacts:\n- In 2013, Koch Industries had revenues of $115 billion and was the second-largest privately owned company in the United States.\n- In 2016, Jane Mayer published the nonfiction book Dark Money: The Hidden History of the Billionaires Behind the Rise of the Radical Right.\n- Dark Money describes a network of extremely wealthy conservative libertarians led foremost by Charles Koch and David Koch.\n- Dark Money says this network funded organizations that worked together to influence academic institutions, think tanks, the courts, statehouses, Congress, and the American presidency for the network's benefit.\n- The Koch family is an American family engaged in business, noted for its political activities and for controlling Koch Industries.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
      {
        "id": 1,
